or\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p><b>Steel Axe</b> is an axe sold at <a href=\"/wiki/The_Oak_Depot\" title=\"The Oak Depot\">The Oak Depot</a> for $5,000. It's a bigger and faster version of a now removed <a href=\"/wiki/Old_Steel_Axe\" title=\"Old Steel Axe\">Old Steel Axe</a>. \n</p><p>A nice and affordable choice for intermediate players. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearance\">Appearance</span></h2>\n<p><b>Steel Axe</b> is a tall hatchet made out of wood and steel. It's headpiece is dark gray in color and uses the default legacy metal texture. Handle, like any other axe, is made out of dark brown wood with default legacy wood material applied to it. At the bottom of it there is a small hole.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>Before v1.52.0 it was named <b>Tall Steel Axe</b></li>\n<li>In the past, there existed a smaller and weaker version of this axe - <a href=\"/wiki/Old_Steel_Axe\" title=\"Old Steel Axe\">Old Steel Axe</a>.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903163625\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 78/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 45/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 11/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.005/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019497/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   28.417      1 Template:Axe\n100.00%   28.417      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved 